   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר אֲפִילּוּ אֵינוֹ מְסוּלָּק מִן הָאָרֶץ וְכוּ׳. דְּבָעֵינַן הַנָּחָה עַל גַּבֵּי מַשֶּׁהוּ.",
   "en": "It was stated in the mishna that «Rabbi Yehuda says: Even» if the scroll «is removed only» a needle breadth «from the ground,» one rolls it back to himself. The Gemara explains: Rabbi Yehuda maintains «that» in order for an object to be deemed at rest, «we require» that it «rest atop something.» Consequently, a scroll that is not actually touching the ground is not considered resting and may be rolled back."
  }
